he Laplace transforms of the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t),$ respectively."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120245 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf29808-4551-56a0-ac86-a4587a06fc0f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line and a Plane Given in Other Forms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a69b22d8-5f30-5e05-81bb-243ed724e1d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,-4, 7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117600} {:answer/id #uuid "cdce1910-9bcc-5251-b118-6aa04aaeb35a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117601} {:answer/id #uuid "06faf094-268f-5487-9e0a-8dda830b16c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-8, 1, 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117602} {:answer/id #uuid "4ea6e821-2c68-5890-9921-7e7988992607" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7,-4, 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117603} {:answer/id #uuid "79a2209b-6180-5a7d-9efd-5b7a99c8eed8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7, 1,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117604}] :answer-field/id #uuid "fe66adf4-1b34-5a67-af27-8e9f1215ce5c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117599}] :question/id #uuid "49e4fa98-401d-5c2d-a49c-1997a8550033" :question/math-academy-id "q-33203" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n$l: r = ⟨ - 5, 0, 1⟩ + t⟨ - 3, 1, 0⟩, Π: - 3x + y - 2z + 27 = 0$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120248 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "930466fc-c7fe-51a5-8634-818abddd0da9" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Principal Normal at a Given Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a874d8e3-9a22-519e-9812-7190479ca678" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}i - \\frac{4}{5}k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117618} {:answer/id #uuid "c84f8d58-bc46-54b6-a742-c27b8da8ade3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5}j - \\frac{4}{5}k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117619} {:answer/id #uuid "e2170b0a-e694-5929-96ce-1fe3794d1111" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}j - \\frac{3}{5}k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117620} {:answer/id #uuid "52575909-820a-5276-b2d2-7400ea1affec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}i + \\frac{4}{5}j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117621} {:answer/id #uuid "5bb4c81a-b3c7-5508-91d2-d81d952a3208" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{5}i - \\frac{3}{5}j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117622}] :answer-field/id #uuid "a053211b-e5f5-5c7e-af98-df1f8ec16472" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117617}] :question/id #uuid "fee02912-87a3-5a99-92ba-f8ae9f270c88" :question/math-academy-id "q-33233" :question/problem "The equations of a curve $r(t)$ and its corresponding unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at an arbitrary point are given below. Find the principal normal vector to that curve at the point $P(0, 3, 4)$.\n$r(t)|= 5\\cos ti + 3\\sin tj + 4\\sin tk, t ∈ [0, 2π); T(t)|=-\\sin ti + \\frac{3}{5}\\cos tj + \\frac{4}{5}\\cos tk, t ∈ [0, 2π)$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390977 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b8d3a6-0298-5f65-ad28-e2fc3cde731d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Tangent to a Trajectory Given an Initial Value Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb3b07ff-aef5-5f25-9d62-58beb7b0a9c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390979} {:answer/id #uuid "c8c7ff40-2935-56f7-9dc2-fe38a0c6ad84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390980} {:answer/id #uuid "79e7bb7a-8936-5e17-8b1f-480cf0b8051d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390981} {:answer/id #uuid "dc205ce9-1943-5f15-9070-06f16eb5285a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390982} {:answer/id #uuid "155c7953-ebd6-5125-950b-0dbf516f6b00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390983}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb3b07ff-aef5-5f25-9d62-58beb7b0a9c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390979} :answer-field/id #uuid "81b19a46-8f9d-50a2-8da7-1578e12a6711" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390978}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "abd93af3-0e28-559c-8c83-70bb59f81df3" :question/math-academy-id "q-332610" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=5x(t)-y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-x(t)-2y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above and its trajectory passing through the point $(1,-1)$ in the phase space of the system. What is the tangent vector to the trajectory at this point?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the $xy$-coordinate plane is called the *phase plane* of the system. A particular solution of an initial value problem is called a *trajectory* (or *orbit*).\n\nIn our case, the trajectory (solution) passes through the point $(x,y)=(1,-1)$ in the phase space. Substituting the coordinates of this point into the equations of our system, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′} & =5x-y \\\\  & =5(1)-(-1) \\\\  & =5+1 \\\\  & =6 \\\\ {y}^{′} & =-x-2y \\\\  & =-1-2(-1) \\\\  & =-1+2 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent vector to the trajectory is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′} \\\\ {y}^{′}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390984 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b8d3a6-0298-5f65-ad28-e2fc3cde731d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Tangent to a Trajectory Given an Initial Value Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f5e819a-7875-572e-8eb2-bb05664a032d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 48\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390986} {:answer/id #uuid "6969347f-013c-5716-b248-5b42f238f060" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 48\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390987} {:answer/id #uuid "1474c3be-2841-59fd-a69b-176b2d5cd24c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390988} {:answer/id #uuid "a6cf9fb9-94c6-575b-a613-48c6446228a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 192\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390989} {:answer/id #uuid "2ad27a47-d093-5c36-a0bf-7265daf0659f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}192 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390990}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6cf9fb9-94c6-575b-a613-48c6446228a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 192\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390989} :answer-field/id #uuid "96925274-8e7d-5159-93dd-aee3f333c8ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390985}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "28e64722-99a7-5d4a-b749-394a97d4ce0b" :question/math-academy-id "q-332616" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]x(t),\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,x(t)={e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{4t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem and its solution given above. What is the tangent vector to the solution curve at the point corresponding to $t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡2?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the $xy$-coordinate plane is called the *phase plane* of the system. A particular solution of an initial value problem is called a *trajectory* (or *orbit*).\n\nFirst, we compute the point that corresponds to $t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$ on the given trajectory:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) & ={e}^{2(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{4(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =4[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+16[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 48\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 48\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation of our system, we obtain the tangent vector to the trajectory.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 48\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2(4)+0(48) \\\\ 0(4)+4(48)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 192\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390991 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b8d3a6-0298-5f65-ad28-e2fc3cde731d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Tangent to a Trajectory Given an Initial Value Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20520810-b4a6-5630-bc41-17cb9d317005" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 72\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390993} {:answer/id #uuid "65e6b3a1-dd4a-5bdb-9ab7-70a3bf5f15eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -72\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390994} {:answer/id #uuid "1f15c7b9-5917-506f-9346-531489dc93ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -36\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390995} {:answer/id #uuid "def0329a-a2e9-56a8-a107-8950057b96f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -36\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390996} {:answer/id #uuid "20bb2938-42f4-5d6f-b5be-8bf12b01f39e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-72 \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390997}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65e6b3a1-dd4a-5bdb-9ab7-70a3bf5f15eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -72\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390994} :answer-field/id #uuid "35839db6-28e1-5c44-9082-b9f7f244356a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390992}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "75adf624-a2db-5ea7-93a2-7ef71176d432" :question/math-academy-id "q-332617" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]x(t),\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],\\,x(t)={e}^{-t}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem and its solution given above. What is the tangent vector to the solution curve at the point corresponding to $t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡3?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the $xy$-coordinate plane is called the *phase plane* of the system. A particular solution of an initial value problem is called a *trajectory* (or *orbit*).\n\nFirst, we compute the point that corresponds to $t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡3$ on the given trajectory:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) & ={e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{2(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+9[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -36\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -36\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation of our system, we obtain the tangent vector to the trajectory.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -36\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(-1)(\\frac{2}{3})+0(-36) \\\\ 0\\cdot (\\frac{2}{3})+2(-36)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -72\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390998 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74b8d3a6-0298-5f65-ad28-e2fc3cde731d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Tangent to a Trajectory Given an Initial Value Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c1207d6-660a-5878-9696-b2a6f678e57f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391000} {:answer/id #uuid "c326cefc-3d33-51f6-b6f0-7a69d00ee5f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391001} {:answer/id #uuid "bb18a87c-c989-5a99-a62f-c5acf7e387f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391002} {:answer/id #uuid "039ed41b-f17e-574f-b5e7-b148acc75dcb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391003} {:answer/id #uuid "a58f61bc-6d44-5e5e-b7a6-0aa84d474cad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391004}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c326cefc-3d33-51f6-b6f0-7a69d00ee5f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391001} :answer-field/id #uuid "491749e3-5dfc-5a6a-8c20-a36eb891b6a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390999}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "be9877ee-3abb-5c56-bc3e-693bac7c1ef7" :question/math-academy-id "q-332619" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]x(t),\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,x(t)={e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem and its solution given above. What is the tangent vector to the solution curve at the point corresponding to $t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡3?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the $xy$-coordinate plane is called the *phase plane* of the system. A particular solution of an initial value problem is called a *trajectory* (or *orbit*).\n\nFirst, we compute the point that corresponds to $t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡3$ on the given trajectory:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) & ={e}^{-2(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+3[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation of our system, we obtain the tangent vector to the trajectory.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2(\\frac{1}{3})+0(6) \\\\ 0(\\frac{1}{3})+1(6)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391005 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d219270-5202-54e6-8cba-dc816155bd7b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Nullclines of a System of Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d7186fc2-d7d8-5021-9db7-19862e6564d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391007} {:answer/id #uuid "7804d689-9587-56c6-9ec2-fc46413ff481" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391008} {:answer/id #uuid "d87b4196-731d-5636-a0e6-fb5cf62cde8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391009} {:answer/id #uuid "9d3186e9-3510-534c-8d19-238c79cedee9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391010}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7804d689-9587-56c6-9ec2-fc46413ff481" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391008} :answer-field/id #uuid "035c96b1-47d3-525c-b3c0-c8ed26f1ce1f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391006} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5db16159-d521-5f88-be7e-27f7a5d92ada" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391012} {:answer/id #uuid "792cb919-03ee-5f97-8075-ab5dac3f04de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391013} {:answer/id #uuid "d0e8806a-4388-56b5-bdc0-9bc7690028dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391014} {:answer/id #uuid "50858950-c939-535a-92dc-1c535cf70804" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391015}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "792cb919-03ee-5f97-8075-ab5dac3f04de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391013} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c9cda5d-a410-57da-87b8-e231cfe1744b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391011}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4465eca2-fa42-514f-bf86-62fcd4c733a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-332639" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=x(t)+2y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-3x(t)+y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. Find equations of the $x$- and $y$-nullclines for the corresponding phase space.\n$\\,$\nThe $x$-nullcline is $y=$ {{field-1}}. \n\n$\\,$\nThe $y$-nullcline is $y=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Recall that: \n\n- The $x$-nullcline is a line for which ${x}^{′}=0$ (i.e., the tangents to trajectories are vertical). So, to find it, we set the first equation of the system equal to $0:$\n\n$$\nx+2y=0\\,⇒\\,y=-\\frac{1}{2}x\n$$\n\n- The $y$-nullcline is a line for which ${y}^{′}=0$ (i.e., the tangents to trajectories are horizontal). So, to find it, we set the second equation of the system equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n-3x+y=0\\,⇒\\,y=3x\n$$\n\nPlotting these in the phase space, we obtain the following:\n\n![](images/b6/b6eb04363e97559b51ae43439d965eb19fd7f6acca57916f3159317ceba033ba.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391016 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d219270-5202-54e6-8cba-dc816155bd7b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Nullclines of a System of Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ffb971ce-3049-51fe-a2a9-c6213cc2efee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391018} {:answer/id #uuid "bf670add-7944-52cc-b5a3-85e4e4a604c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391019} {:answer/id #uuid "bb4b7a2a-e2e0-587f-89c2-2aaafeb3f74e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391020} {:answer/id #uuid "99569669-a543-5340-987b-9fc9931edc10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391021}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf670add-7944-52cc-b5a3-85e4e4a604c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391019} :answer-field/id #uuid "61a88848-0820-56d5-8abf-a85a11640c85" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391017} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a44db6a6-2316-5d2c-8d64-0db34ccee926" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391023} {:answer/id #uuid "d2157be3-cbfc-59ce-9f32-0279b2cb490e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391024} {:answer/id #uuid "0fd45b74-ec56-5bae-afc9-e9351e6d106e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391025} {:answer/id #uuid "d74c784d-bc11-5a4e-81c2-e3b3a5111808" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391026}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d74c784d-bc11-5a4e-81c2-e3b3a5111808" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391026} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1143ad8-a7c5-5043-8f31-4c5191cbed01" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391022}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5e7fabf8-a5ca-5309-a7c3-5690ee882dd5" :question/math-academy-id "q-332651" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-3x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=5x(t)+y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. Find equations of the $x$- and $y$-nullclines for the corresponding phase space.$\\,$\nThe $x$-nullcline is $y=$ {{field-1}}. \n\n$\\,$\nThe $y$-nullcline is $y=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Recall that: \n\n- The $x$-nullcline is a line for which ${x}^{′}=0$ (i.e., the tangents to trajectories are vertical). So, to find it, we set the first equation of the system equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n-3x+y=0\\,⇒\\,y=3x\n$$\n\n- The $y$-nullcline is a line for which ${y}^{′}=0$ (i.e., the tangents to trajectories are horizontal). So, to find it, we set the second equation of the system equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n5x+y=0\\,⇒\\,y=-5x\n$$\n\nPlotting these in the phase space, we obtain the following:\n\n![](images/c5/c5bbfde035449e1495b02d71a2b1199bf0dbaf7388e0c8eefa1e40e0816fdf7a.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391027 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d219270-5202-54e6-8cba-dc816155bd7b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Nullclines of a System of Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14cc3e70-6b95-5c01-9229-5253469d00f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391029} {:answer/id #uuid "22ff70ec-9701-5e8f-abd1-2d858845aef0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391030} {:answer/id #uuid "3df30548-d12d-59eb-a9b4-29aeaa3bf339" :answer/type {:db/i